<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mrs. Wells returns two weeks after her first visit with her home blood pressure log and the outside report she obtained: two years ago another clinic measured her creatinine at 1.05 mg/dL and reported an eGFR of 64 as normal. That report used an older equation that raised the estimate for Black patients; recalculated with the race-free CKD-EPI 1926 equation it is 59, already reduced, and no urine albumin test was done then. Her home readings over seven days average 150/88. She stopped naproxen at the first visit and uses acetaminophen for her knees, which works. Her ankles still swell a little by evening and she is still tired in the afternoons. She had her kidney ultrasound this morning and saw Dr. Lindqvist-Moore of nephrology afterwards. She asked to see each calculation and was given copies. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Home blood pressure</td><td>Average 150/88 over seven days</td></tr><tr><td>Earlier result</td><td>Creatinine 1.05 two years ago, reported with a race-adjusted eGFR of 64; race-free eGFR 59</td></tr><tr><td>Naproxen</td><td>Stopped; acetaminophen instead</td></tr><tr><td>Symptoms</td><td>Tiredness and evening ankle swelling, unchanged</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.18"/>
    <code code="10187-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Review of systems Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Review of Systems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Result</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Constitutional</td><td>Positive</td><td>Tired in the afternoons; no fever or weight loss</td></tr><tr><td>Cardiovascular</td><td>Positive</td><td>Mild ankle swelling by evening; no chest pain or breathlessness lying flat</td></tr><tr><td>Genitourinary</td><td>Negative</td><td>No blood in the urine, foamy urine, or burning</td></tr><tr><td>Musculoskeletal</td><td>Positive</td><td>Knee aching, controlled with acetaminophen</td></tr><tr><td>Integumentary</td><td>Negative</td><td>No rash or itching</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>5 systems reviewed. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

